# Audit O6: one line-ending rule for every machine.
#
# The repository already stores text as LF. Without this file, a Windows clone
# with core.autocrlf=true checks files out as CRLF, and the tests that compare
# a rendered document byte-for-byte with the committed one fail locally while
# passing on CI. `eol=lf` makes the working tree match the repository
# everywhere, regardless of each contributor's git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep the line endings their interpreters expect.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.docx binary
